module sh.sysl.compiler

import sysl.buf.{Buf, buf}
import sysl.container.{Map, map, Set, set}
import sysl.text.Search

// **A share of something a held local already keeps alive is no share at all**, wherever in the
// function it is given back.
//
// Taking a slice of a slice retains the owner, and the end of the new slice's scope releases it. Where
// the parent is a parameter or a `val` -- a stack slot nothing outside the frame can name, written
// once -- the parent's own count keeps the owner alive for as long as the parent is in scope, so a
// view taken from it and given back before the parent is needs no count of its own. `arc_elide.sysl`
// cancels a pair inside one basic block; a view taken in a loop and walked by a `for` is given back
// blocks later, past the loop that read it, and is the shape this pass is for:
//
//     while i + most <= src.len
//         val here = src[i..<i + most]     // retain src's owner
//         for x in here ...
//         i += most                        // release here's owner, every round
//
// **The rule.** A retain of a reference read out of a *covering* slot is dropped with every release
// that gives its count back when, on every path from the retain, one of those releases comes before
// the function returns, before the retain runs again, before the slot is written and before any
// other release. A slot covers when nothing outside the frame can reach it, it is stored to exactly
// once, and the value stored holds a count: a parameter (its caller's, or the one the function took
// for it), or a value whose count was taken just before the store.
//
// **What gives the count back** is followed through field reads and field writes, and through loads
// of the one slot the new value was stored into: a release whose reference was put together by the
// retain's own value, or read from that slot, gives back the retained count.
//
// **A count is observable**, so the window must not look at it: `slot_vacate` lets storage go only
// where the strong count is one, and a share dropped from under a view would let it free slots the
// view still reads. What may sit in the window is listed at `count_blind`; a call to anything that
// could release or write outside its own frame, and any other release (a destructor is such code),
// keeps the pair.
//
// **Why it is sound.** The slot's count holds the object alive from before the retain until after the
// last release dropped, so the count never reaches zero inside the window, nothing inside reads it,
// and outside it the count is what it was. Each path loses one retain and the one release that gave
// it back, so no count ends anywhere else and no destructor moves.
//
// **A share of a reference read out of storage that is not a slot of this frame** -- a field of what a
// parameter refers to, an element of a buffer, the payload of the enum a `match` is looking at -- is
// dropped by the same rule, and so is the one share of a tuple or struct put together on the spot from
// such reads (`m.get((n.a, n.b))`, `val (a, b) = (xs[i], xs[j])`). What that leans on is not a slot
// of the frame but the window itself. The reference is alive when the retain runs, or the retain
// would be touching freed memory, so its count is at least one there; a count only falls at a
// release, and the window holds none -- a callee in it is one that releases nothing it did not take,
// and so lets nothing reach zero. So the count stays at least one to the release that ends the window,
// is read by nothing in between, and is the same after it as with both kept. That holds for whoever
// else holds the object, which is why the place the reference came from need not stay put; what it
// needs is that no other code runs in the window at all:
//
// - **a coroutine's suspension point, or the resumption of an awaited task,** hands the thread to other
//   tasks of the domain, which may write the place and give back what it held, so a window over one is
//   refused (`suspends`). A slot of the frame is out of their reach, but a count is not -- they may
//   look at it -- so a covering slot's window is refused there too.
// - **another thread** reaches such storage only under its lock (a `&T` never leaves its domain, and
//   what a `&sync T` shares is not safe to mutate without one), and taking or giving back a lock is a
//   call that ends the window; a reference read and given back with no lock between them by two
//   threads at once is a data race whether the share is taken or not.
// - **an interrupt handler** shares storage with the program through `volatile`, and a volatile read
//   is no plain load, so a reference read out of one is never in a window. A plain variable both sides
//   write is one the optimizer is already entitled to read once, and the program's own read of it
//   races the handler with or without the share.
//
// A slot of this frame is still asked whether it covers: written once, with a value holding a count.
// The frame keeps values there it took no count for -- a borrowed argument, the destination of a share
// this pass already dropped -- and the narrower question is the one those were proved against.

// Where a value comes from: the value a walk back through field reads and writes stopped at, the
// field of it (each index followed by a `.`), and the field writes it passed (`|name|`). Values are
// named as they print (`%t7`), which is how `defs` is keyed.
private struct Origin
    leaf: string
    path: string
    through: string

private index_text(idx: Buf[int]) -> string
    var s = ""

    for k in idx
        s = s"$s$k."

    s
end index_text

// The origin of field `path` of `v`, followed back through `extractvalue` and `insertvalue`.
private origin_of(defs: Map[string, Inst], v: Val, path: string, through: string) -> Origin
    val n = v_render(v)

    defs.get(n) match
        Some(InExtract(_, _, agg, idx)) -> origin_of(defs, agg, s"${index_text(idx)}$path", through)
        Some(InInsert(_, _, agg, _, value, idx)) ->
            val at = index_text(idx)

            if path.starts_with(at)
                origin_of(defs, value, path[at.bytes.len..<path.bytes.len], s"$through|$n|")
            else if at.starts_with(path) then Origin(n, path, through)
            else origin_of(defs, agg, path, through)
        _ -> Origin(n, path, through)
end origin_of

// `origin_of` from the whole of `v`, as the value it stopped at, the field of it and the field writes
// passed (`arc_take.sysl`).
value_origin(defs: Map[string, Inst], v: Val) -> (string, string, string)
    val o = origin_of(defs, v, "", "")

    (o.leaf, o.path, o.through)
end value_origin

// The slot a plain load `leaf` read, or "".
private loaded_slot(defs: Map[string, Inst], leaf: string) -> string = defs.get(leaf) match
    Some(InLoad(_, _, p, acc, _)) if is_plain_access(acc) -> v_render(p)
    _ -> ""

// Where a slot is stored to: its block, its index, the value. More than one store is no slot this
// pass reads.
private struct SlotStore
    block: usize
    at: usize
    value: Val
    count: int

// A retain this pass may drop: where it is, the release that gives its count back, the slot whose
// count covers it and the field of the slot the reference is, the field writes that put the reference
// into a new value, and the slot that new value was stored into ("" for none) with the field of it.
// `held` is the slot of the frame whose own count holds the reference, where it was read through a
// place entry out of that slot's bytes ("" for none): what lets a release sit in the window.
private struct Cover
    block: usize
    at: usize
    release: string
    slot: string
    path: string
    leaf: string
    inserts: Set[string]
    into: string
    into_path: string
    held: string

// What a window holding a release asks: the release helpers' walks, and the slots of the frame read
// only through a place entry answering in their own bytes, by the register each such call answered.
private struct Reach
    walks: Map[string, ReleaseWalk]
    placed: Map[string, string]

// **What `cover_at` asks of a block, found by key instead of by walking the block**: once per retain,
// a walk of the rest of its block (for the stores and field writes its share goes into) or of the
// block up to a slot's store (for the count the slot holds) is a cost that grows with the square of
// a long block -- an entry file's body with thousands of statements is one. Each list is ascending.
//
// - `retains`: the first retain or copy of an origin in a block, by `site_key(b, leaf, path)`.
// - `stores`: the stores of a block whose value may carry a reference out of `leaf`, by `"b|leaf"` --
//   every value the walk back from the stored value meets (`reached`), which holds every leaf
//   `carried` can answer.
// - `inserts`: the field writes of a block of a value, by `"b|value"`.
//
// And what `window_ends` asks, where a walk on from each retain to the end of its window is the same
// square: the first instruction at or after each one that ends any window (`stops[b][i]`: neither
// blind to counts nor a release, or a suspension), the stores of a block to a pointer (`stored_to`,
// `"b|ptr"`), the instructions that read, write or hand on a slot (`touched`, `"b|slot"`, every root
// `rooted_at` answers for), and the releases of a block (`releases`, by `"b"`), of an origin's leaf
// (`"b|leaf"`) and of a value read out of a slot (`"b|=slot"`) -- the only ones `gives_back` can match.
private struct Sites
    retains: Map[string, usize]
    stores: Lists
    inserts: Lists
    stops: Buf[Buf[usize]]
    stored_to: Lists
    touched: Lists
    releases: Lists

// Lists of instruction indexes by key, each in the order noted.
private struct Lists
    slot: Map[string, usize]
    at: Buf[Buf[usize]]

    note(*self, key: string, j: usize)
        self.slot.get(key) match
            Some(i) -> self.at[i].push(j)
            None ->
                var one: Buf[usize] = buf()

                one.push(j)
                self.slot.put(key, self.at.len())
                self.at.push(one)

    // The indexes noted under `key` in `lo..<hi`, in order.
    within(self, key: string, lo: usize, hi: usize) -> Buf[usize]
        var out: Buf[usize] = buf()

        self.slot.get(key) match
            Some(i) ->
                val xs = self.at[i]

                for k in first_at_least(xs, lo)..<xs.len()
                    if xs[k] >= hi then break

                    out.push(xs[k])
            None -> ()

        out

    // The first index noted under `key` in `lo..<hi`, or `hi`.
    first(self, key: string, lo: usize, hi: usize) -> usize = self.slot.get(key) match
        Some(i) ->
            val xs = self.at[i]
            val k = first_at_least(xs, lo)

            if k < xs.len() && xs[k] < hi then xs[k] else hi
        None -> hi
end Lists

// Where in the ascending `xs` the first value at least `lo` is (`xs.len()` for none).
private first_at_least(xs: Buf[usize], lo: usize) -> usize
    var a: usize = 0
    var b = xs.len()

    while a < b
        val m = a + (b - a) / 2

        if xs[m] < lo then a = m + 1 else b = m

    a
end first_at_least

private site_key(b: usize, leaf: string, path: string) -> string = s"$b|$leaf|$path"

// The first retain or copy of each origin in each block, by `site_key` (`Sites.retains`).
private first_retains(blocks: Buf[IrBlock], defs: Map[string, Inst]) -> Map[string, usize]
    var retains: Map[string, usize] = map()

    for b in 0..<blocks.len()
        val instrs = blocks[b].instrs

        for i in 0..<instrs.len()
            arc_call_of(instrs[i]) match
                Some((name, v)) ->
                    if name != "arc.weak_retain" && release_for(name).is_some()
                        val o = origin_of(defs, v, "", "")
                        val k = site_key(b, o.leaf, o.path)

                        if !retains.has(k) then retains.put(k, i)
                None -> ()

    retains
end first_retains

// Whether a retain of the value at `o` is among the first `n` instructions of block `b`.
private taken_in(retains: Map[string, usize], b: usize, n: usize, o: Origin) -> bool =
    retains.get(site_key(b, o.leaf, o.path)).map(j -> j < n).unwrap_or(false)

private sites_of(blocks: Buf[IrBlock], defs: Map[string, Inst], inert: Set[string], reach: Reach,
                 retains: Map[string, usize]) -> Sites
    var stores = Lists(map(), buf())
    var inserts = Lists(map(), buf())
    var stops: Buf[Buf[usize]] = buf()
    var stored_to = Lists(map(), buf())
    var touched = Lists(map(), buf())
    var releases = Lists(map(), buf())

    for b in 0..<blocks.len()
        val instrs = blocks[b].instrs
        var stopping: Buf[bool] = buf()

        for i in 0..<instrs.len()
            val inst = instrs[i]
            var released = false

            inst match
                InInsert(_, _, _, _, v, _) -> inserts.note(s"$b|${v_render(v)}", i)
                InStore(_, v, p, _, _) ->
                    for leaf in reached(defs, v)
                        stores.note(s"$b|$leaf", i)

                    stored_to.note(s"$b|${v_render(p)}", i)
                _ ->
                    arc_call_of(inst) match
                        Some((name, v)) ->
                            if is_release(name)
                                val o = origin_of(defs, v, "", "")
                                val slot = loaded_slot(defs, o.leaf)

                                released = true
                                releases.note(s"$b", i)
                                releases.note(s"$b|${o.leaf}", i)

                                if slot != "" then releases.note(s"$b|=$slot", i)
                        None -> ()

            for s in touched_roots(defs, reach, inst)
                touched.note(s"$b|$s", i)

            stopping.push(!released && (!count_blind(defs, inert, inst) || suspends(inst)))

        var next: Buf[usize] = buf()
        var at = instrs.len()

        for k in 0..<instrs.len()
            next.push(0)

        for k in 0..<instrs.len()
            val i = instrs.len() - 1 - k

            if stopping[i] then at = i

            next[i] = at

        stops.push(next)

    Sites(retains, stores, inserts, stops, stored_to, touched, releases)
end sites_of

// Every slot `inst` reads, writes or hands on: the roots (`rooted_at`) of what it loads from or stores
// to, and of every operand it hands on.
private touched_roots(defs: Map[string, Inst], reach: Reach, inst: Inst) -> Buf[string]
    var out: Buf[string] = buf()

    inst match
        InLoad(_, _, p, _, _) ->
            roots_into(defs, reach, p, &out)
            return out
        InStore(_, _, p, _, _) -> roots_into(defs, reach, p, &out)
        _ -> ()

    for v in escaping_operands(inst)
        roots_into(defs, reach, v, &out)

    out
end touched_roots

// Every `s` that `rooted_at(defs, reach, v, s)` answers true for.
private roots_into(defs: Map[string, Inst], reach: Reach, v: Val, out: *Buf[string])
    var cur = v

    loop
        val n = v_render(cur)

        out.push(n)

        reach.placed.get(n) match
            Some(s) -> out.push(s)
            None -> ()

        defs.get(n) match
            Some(InGep(_, _, p, _)) -> cur = p
            Some(InGepInBounds(_, _, p, _)) -> cur = p
            _ -> return
end roots_into

// Every value a walk back from `v` through `extractvalue` and `insertvalue` meets, `v` among them: the
// values `origin_of` from `v` can stop at, whatever the field asked for.
private reached(defs: Map[string, Inst], v: Val) -> Buf[string]
    var out: Buf[string] = buf()
    var seen: Set[string] = set()
    var work: Buf[Val] = buf()

    work.push(v)

    while !work.is_empty()
        val cur = work.pop().unwrap()
        val n = v_render(cur)

        if seen.has(n) then continue

        seen.add(n)
        out.push(n)

        defs.get(n) match
            Some(InExtract(_, _, agg, _)) -> work.push(agg)
            Some(InInsert(_, _, agg, _, value, _)) ->
                work.push(agg)
                work.push(value)
            _ -> ()

    out
end reached

elide_covered(blocks: Buf[IrBlock], clean: Set[string], inert: Set[string], walks: Map[string, ReleaseWalk],
              own: Map[string, int]) -> Buf[IrBlock]
    var defs: Map[string, Inst] = map()
    var stores: Map[string, SlotStore] = map()
    var labels: Map[string, usize] = map()

    for b in 0..<blocks.len()
        labels.put(blocks[b].label, b)

        val instrs = blocks[b].instrs

        for i in 0..<instrs.len()
            val inst = instrs[i]

            inst match
                InLoad(d, _, _, _, _) -> defs.put(v_render(d), inst)
                InGep(d, _, _, _) -> defs.put(v_render(d), inst)
                InGepInBounds(d, _, _, _) -> defs.put(v_render(d), inst)
                InAlloca(d, _, _) -> defs.put(v_render(d), inst)
                InExtract(d, _, _, _) -> defs.put(v_render(d), inst)
                InInsert(d, _, _, _, _, _) -> defs.put(v_render(d), inst)
                // A place entry's answer, for `count_blind`'s loads through it, and a +0 entry's, which
                // is read out of storage (`zero_entry.sysl`).
                InCall(Some(d), _, VGlobal(callee), _, _, _, _, _) ->
                    if is_place_symbol(callee) || is_zero_symbol(callee) then defs.put(v_render(d), inst)
                // A table's +0 slot's answer, called through the register it was loaded into
                // (`table_zero.sysl`).
                InCall(Some(d), _, VReg(callee), _, _, _, _, _) ->
                    if is_zero_symbol(callee) then defs.put(v_render(d), inst)
                InStore(_, v, p, _, _) ->
                    val slot = v_render(p)

                    if clean.has(slot)
                        stores.get(slot) match
                            Some(s) -> stores.put(slot, s with { count = s.count + 1 })
                            None -> stores.put(slot, SlotStore(b, i, v, 1))
                _ -> ()

    val retains = first_retains(blocks, defs)
    val reach = Reach(walks, held_slots(blocks, defs, own, retains))
    val sites = sites_of(blocks, defs, inert, reach, retains)
    var dropped: Set[string] = set()
    var claimed: Set[string] = set()

    for b in 0..<blocks.len()
        val instrs = blocks[b].instrs

        for i in 0..<instrs.len()
            cover_at(blocks, defs, stores, clean, reach, sites, b, i) match
                Some(c) ->
                    val ends = window_ends(blocks, defs, labels, reach, sites, c)

                    if !ends.is_empty()
                        var fresh = true

                        for e in ends
                            if claimed.has(e) then fresh = false

                        if fresh
                            dropped.add(s"$b:$i")

                            for e in ends
                                claimed.add(e)
                                dropped.add(e)
                None -> ()

    if dropped.len() == 0 then return blocks

    var out: Buf[IrBlock] = buf()

    for b in 0..<blocks.len()
        var kept: Buf[Inst] = buf()
        val instrs = blocks[b].instrs

        for i in 0..<instrs.len()
            if !dropped.has(s"$b:$i") then kept.push(instrs[i])

        out.push(IrBlock(blocks[b].label, kept, blocks[b].terminator))

    out
end elide_covered

// The retain at `blocks[b].instrs[i]`, if it is one of a reference read out of a covering slot or out
// of storage, or the copy of a value put together from such reads, whose new count goes nowhere but
// into values and one clean slot.
private cover_at(blocks: Buf[IrBlock], defs: Map[string, Inst], stores: Map[string, SlotStore],
                 clean: Set[string], reach: Reach, sites: Sites, b: usize, i: usize) -> Option[Cover]
    val (name, x) = arc_call_of(blocks[b].instrs[i])?

    if name == "arc.weak_retain" then return None

    val release = release_for(name)?
    // The reference may have been put into a value already, by the field writes of an earlier share;
    // what it is a field of is what it was read out of.
    val from = origin_of(defs, x, "", "")
    val slot = loaded_slot(defs, from.leaf)

    // A slot of the frame must cover it. Any other place the reference was read out of -- a field, an
    // element, the payload of the enum a `match` is looking at -- needs only the window, and so does a
    // value built on the spot out of such reads (see the head of this file).
    //
    // **What a +0 entry answers is such a read too** (`zero_entry.sysl`): references read out of the
    // storage of an argument, by a body that released nothing, so each is alive when the retain runs.
    if slot == ""
        if !zero_answer(defs, from) && (!name.starts_with("arc.copy.") ||
                                         !built_of_places(blocks, defs, stores, clean, sites, x)) then
            return None
    else if !held_where_read(defs, stores, clean, sites, from)
        return None

    val instrs = blocks[b].instrs
    var inserts: Set[string] = set()
    var into = ""
    var into_path = ""

    // The rest of the block's field writes of `x`, and its stores of a value that may carry it
    // (`Sites`): no other store can, so the walk of the block they stand for meets these alone.
    for j in sites.inserts.within(s"$b|${v_render(x)}", i + 1, instrs.len())
        instrs[j] match
            InInsert(d, _, _, _, _, _) -> inserts.add(v_render(d))
            _ -> ()

    for j in sites.stores.within(s"$b|${from.leaf}", i + 1, instrs.len())
        instrs[j] match
            InStore(_, v, p, _, _) ->
                carried(defs, v, from) match
                    Some(at) ->
                        val target = v_render(p)
                        val s = stores.get(target)

                        if into != "" || !clean.has(target) || s.is_none() || s.unwrap().count != 1 then return None

                        into = target
                        into_path = at
                    None -> ()
            _ -> ()

    // A reference read through a place entry out of the bytes of a slot that holds a count on all it is
    // ever given is held by that count (`held_slots`).
    val held = if slot == "" then "" else reach.placed.get(slot).unwrap_or("")

    Some(Cover(b, i, release, slot, from.path, from.leaf, inserts, into, into_path, held))
end cover_at

// Whether the reference at `from` is what a +0 entry answered, or a part of it.
private zero_answer(defs: Map[string, Inst], from: Origin) -> bool = defs.get(from.leaf) match
    Some(InCall(_, _, VGlobal(callee), _, _, _, _, _)) -> is_zero_symbol(callee)
    Some(InCall(_, _, VReg(callee), _, _, _, _, _)) -> is_zero_symbol(callee)
    _ -> false

// Whether `v` is a value put together on the spot by field writes into nothing, each counted field
// written with something read out of a place (or itself put together the same way): a tuple or a
// struct built of fields and elements, whose share is one share of each of those places' references.
// A field of a plain number counts nothing; any other value -- a call's result, a fresh box, a
// constant -- is a count no place holds, and keeps the share.
private built_of_places(blocks: Buf[IrBlock], defs: Map[string, Inst], stores: Map[string, SlotStore],
                        clean: Set[string], sites: Sites, v: Val) -> bool
    var cur = v
    var fields = 0

    loop
        defs.get(v_render(cur)) match
            Some(InInsert(_, _, agg, vty, value, _)) ->
                val counted = vty match
                    LInt(_) -> false
                    LFloat(_, _) -> false
                    _ -> true

                if counted
                    val from = origin_of(defs, value, "", "")
                    val read = if loaded_slot(defs, from.leaf) == "" then false
                               else held_where_read(defs, stores, clean, sites, from)

                    if !read && !built_of_places(blocks, defs, stores, clean, sites, value) then return false

                fields += 1
                cur = agg
            _ -> break

    if fields == 0 then return false

    cur match
        VUndef -> true
        VZero -> true
        VPoison -> true
        _ -> false
end built_of_places

// Whether the place the reference at `from` was read out of holds a count on it. A slot of this frame
// does when it covers: written once, with a value that holds a count. Any other place -- a field, an
// element, a global, a slot whose address has left the frame -- is storage the reference was kept
// in, and storage keeps a count on what it holds.
private held_where_read(defs: Map[string, Inst], stores: Map[string, SlotStore], clean: Set[string], sites: Sites,
                        from: Origin) -> bool
    val slot = loaded_slot(defs, from.leaf)

    if !clean.has(slot) then return true

    stores.get(slot) match
        Some(held) -> held.count == 1 && holds_a_count(defs, sites, held, from.path)
        None -> false
end held_where_read

// Whether the one value stored to a covering slot holds a count on field `path`: a parameter does,
// and so does a value whose field had a count taken for it earlier in the store's own block.
private holds_a_count(defs: Map[string, Inst], sites: Sites, held: SlotStore, path: string) -> bool
    held.value match
        VReg(n) -> if held.block == 0 && n.ends_with(".param") then return true
        _ -> ()

    val want = origin_of(defs, held.value, path, "")
    // A copy of the whole value takes a count on every field of it.
    val whole = origin_of(defs, held.value, "", "")

    // A retain of either before the store, found by the first one of each in the block (`Sites`).
    taken_before(sites, held, want) || taken_before(sites, held, whole)
end holds_a_count

private taken_before(sites: Sites, held: SlotStore, o: Origin) -> bool =
    taken_in(sites.retains, held.block, held.at, o)

// The field of `v` that holds the reference `xs` (read out of `from`), if `v` carries it: a value
// built by writing it into a field, or a read of the slot field it is part of.
private carried(defs: Map[string, Inst], v: Val, from: Origin) -> Option[string]
    if same_place(origin_of(defs, v, "", ""), from) then return Some("")

    var cur = v

    loop
        defs.get(v_render(cur)) match
            Some(InInsert(_, _, agg, _, _, idx)) ->
                val at = index_text(idx)

                if same_place(origin_of(defs, v, at, ""), from) then return Some(at)

                cur = agg
                continue
            _ -> ()

        break

    val o = origin_of(defs, cur, "", "")

    if o.leaf == from.leaf && from.path.starts_with(o.path)
        val at = from.path[o.path.bytes.len..<from.path.bytes.len]

        if same_place(origin_of(defs, v, at, ""), from) then return Some(at)

    None
end carried

private same_place(a: Origin, b: Origin) -> bool = a.leaf == b.leaf && a.path == b.path

// Every release that gives back the count `c` took, as `block:index`, when each path from the retain
// reaches one before it returns, runs the retain again, gives back the covering slot's own count or
// stores to that slot; otherwise nothing.
private window_ends(blocks: Buf[IrBlock], defs: Map[string, Inst], labels: Map[string, usize], reach: Reach,
                     sites: Sites, c: Cover) -> Buf[string]
    var ends: Buf[string] = buf()
    var end_names: Buf[string] = buf()
    var others: Buf[(string, Val)] = buf()
    var none: Buf[string] = buf()
    var seen: Set[usize] = set()
    var work: Buf[(usize, usize)] = buf()

    work.push((c.block, c.at + 1))

    // Each block's stretch is found by key (`Sites`), not walked: where it stops, the release that gives
    // the share back before that, and only then the other releases in it.
    while !work.is_empty()
        val (b, start) = work.pop().unwrap()
        val instrs = blocks[b].instrs
        val len = instrs.len()

        // The first instruction that ends the window empty-handed: the retain itself come round again,
        // a store to the covering slot, a touch of the slot whose count holds the reference (no store
        // to it, and no read of it, which could hand its count on), or anything not blind to counts.
        var stop = if start < len then sites.stops[b][start] else len

        if b == c.block && c.at >= start && c.at < stop then stop = c.at

        if c.slot != "" then stop = sites.stored_to.first(s"$b|${c.slot}", start, stop)

        if c.held != "" then stop = sites.touched.first(s"$b|${c.held}", start, stop)

        // The release that gives the share back ends the window. Any other is judged once the window is
        // known (`holds_across`): it may let go of nothing the share could be, or the share may be held
        // by a slot's count it cannot give back.
        var closing = stop

        for i in sites.releases.within(s"$b|${c.leaf}", start, stop)
            if i < closing && gives_back_at(defs, c, instrs[i]) then closing = i

        if c.into != ""
            for i in sites.releases.within(s"$b|=${c.into}", start, stop)
                if i < closing && gives_back_at(defs, c, instrs[i]) then closing = i

        if closing == stop && stop < len then return none

        // A window running off the block's end goes on only through a branch; anything else ends it.
        if closing == stop
            blocks[b].terminator match
                Some(InBr(_)) -> ()
                Some(InCondBr(_, _, _)) -> ()
                Some(InSwitch(_, _, _, _)) -> ()
                Some(InUnreachable) -> ()
                _ -> return none

        for i in sites.releases.within(s"$b", start, closing)
            arc_call_of(instrs[i]) match
                Some(other) -> others.push(other)
                None -> ()

        if closing < stop
            ends.push(s"$b:$closing")
            end_names.push(arc_call_of(instrs[closing]).unwrap().0)
            continue
        end if

        var next: Buf[string] = buf()

        blocks[b].terminator match
            Some(InBr(l)) -> next.push(l)
            Some(InCondBr(_, t, f)) ->
                next.push(t)
                next.push(f)
            Some(InSwitch(_, _, d, cases)) ->
                next.push(d)

                for k in cases
                    next.push(k.1)
            Some(InUnreachable) -> ()
            _ -> return none

        for l in next
            labels.get(l) match
                Some(to) ->
                    if !seen.has(to)
                        seen.add(to)
                        work.push((to, 0))
                None -> return none

    for o in others
        if !holds_across(defs, reach, c, end_names, o.0, o.1) then return none

    ends
end window_ends

// Whether the share `c` takes may go although the release `name` of `v` runs inside its window. That
// release runs no code -- no destructor, no trait object's or task's teardown, nothing that could read
// a count or write a place -- and either:
//
// - **the reference is held by a slot of the frame** (`c.held`) that holds a count on all it is ever
//   given, is neither written nor read in the window, and is not what `v` was read out of: the release
//   gives back some other count, and whatever it lets go of, the slot's count keeps the object; or
// - **nothing the release can let go of is of the share's type**: its teardown, followed down every
//   reference it holds, never reaches an object the share could be, so it cannot take that count.
//
// Either way the count stays at least one to the window's end, as with no release in it.
private holds_across(defs: Map[string, Inst], reach: Reach, c: Cover, end_names: Buf[string], name: string,
                     v: Val) -> bool
    val w = reach.walks.get(name) match
        Some(found) -> found
        None -> return false

    if w.code then return false

    if c.held != "" then return !fed_from(defs, reach, v, c.held, 0)

    if w.wide || end_names.is_empty() then return false

    for closing in end_names
        if closing.starts_with("arc.release.")
            if w.keys.has(closing[12..<closing.bytes.len]) then return false
        else if closing.starts_with("arc.dispose.")
            val shared = reach.walks.get(closing) match
                Some(found) -> found
                None -> return false

            if shared.wide then return false

            for k in shared.keys
                if w.keys.has(k) then return false
        else
            return false

    true
end holds_across

// **The slots of the frame whose own count holds what is read out of them**, by the register each
// place call reading one answered. Such a slot is handed to nothing but a place entry answering an
// address in the bytes it was handed (`own`, `place_entry.sysl`'s `in_own_storage`) -- which writes
// nothing -- and that address is only loaded from; every store to it is of the whole value, and the
// value stored holds a count on everything in it (`stored_counted`). A `var` given a value read out of
// storage, as Richards' `run_task` gives `message` the old `self.input`, is one.
private held_slots(blocks: Buf[IrBlock], defs: Map[string, Inst], own: Map[string, int],
                   retains: Map[string, usize]) -> Map[string, string]
    var placed: Map[string, string] = map()
    var calls: Buf[string] = buf()

    if own.is_empty() then return placed

    var slots: Set[string] = set()

    for b in blocks
        for inst in b.instrs
            inst match
                InAlloca(d, _, _) -> slots.add(v_render(d))
                InCall(Some(d), _, VGlobal(callee), args, _, _, _, _) ->
                    val k = own.get(callee).unwrap_or(-1)

                    if k >= 0 && usize(k) < args.len()
                        val s = v_render(args[usize(k)].value)

                        if slots.has(s)
                            placed.put(v_render(d), s)
                            calls.push(v_render(d))
                _ -> ()

    if placed.is_empty() then return placed

    var out_of_reach: Set[string] = set()

    for b in 0..<blocks.len()
        val instrs = blocks[b].instrs

        for i in 0..<instrs.len()
            val inst = instrs[i]
            var at_k = ""

            inst match
                InCall(Some(d), _, VGlobal(_), args, _, _, _, _) -> if placed.has(v_render(d)) then at_k = placed.get(v_render(d)).unwrap()
                InStore(_, v, p, _, _) ->
                    val target = v_render(p)

                    if placed.has(target) then out_of_reach.add(placed.get(target).unwrap())
                    if slots.has(target) && !stored_counted(defs, retains, b, i, v) then out_of_reach.add(target)
                _ -> ()

            var first = at_k != ""

            for v in escaping_operands(inst)
                val n = v_render(v)

                // The one argument of a place call that is the slot it reads, once.
                if first && n == at_k
                    first = false
                    continue

                if slots.has(n) then out_of_reach.add(n)
                if placed.has(n) then out_of_reach.add(placed.get(n).unwrap())

        blocks[b].terminator match
            Some(t) ->
                for v in escaping_operands(t)
                    val n = v_render(v)

                    if slots.has(n) then out_of_reach.add(n)
                    if placed.has(n) then out_of_reach.add(placed.get(n).unwrap())
            None -> ()

    var held: Map[string, string] = map()

    for d in calls
        val s = placed.get(d).unwrap()

        if !out_of_reach.has(s) then held.put(d, s)

    held
end held_slots

// Whether the value `v` stored at `blocks[b].instrs[i]` holds a count on everything in it: a constant
// that holds nothing, or a value a count was taken for earlier in the store's block (the pass runs
// before `arc_fastpath.sysl` puts a copy behind its tag test). A parameter is not taken as one: what a
// borrowed one holds is its caller's.
// Found by the first retain of the value in the block (`first_retains`), not by a walk of the block up
// to the store, which costs the square of a long block.
private stored_counted(defs: Map[string, Inst], retains: Map[string, usize], b: usize, i: usize, v: Val) -> bool =
    v match
        VZero -> true
        VNull -> true
        VUndef -> true
        VPoison -> true
        VReg(_) -> taken_in(retains, b, i, origin_of(defs, v, "", ""))
        _ -> false

// Whether the address `v` is the slot `s` or lies in it: a field address of it, or what a place entry
// answered on it.
private rooted_at(defs: Map[string, Inst], reach: Reach, v: Val, s: string) -> bool
    val n = v_render(v)

    if n == s || reach.placed.get(n).unwrap_or("") == s then return true

    defs.get(n) match
        Some(InGep(_, _, p, _)) -> rooted_at(defs, reach, p, s)
        Some(InGepInBounds(_, _, p, _)) -> rooted_at(defs, reach, p, s)
        _ -> false
end rooted_at

// Whether the release `inst` gives back the count `c` took.
private gives_back_at(defs: Map[string, Inst], c: Cover, inst: Inst) -> bool = arc_call_of(inst) match
    Some((name, v)) -> releases_as(c.release, name) && gives_back(defs, c, origin_of(defs, v, "", ""))
    None -> false

// Whether any part of the value `v` was read out of the slot `s`: followed back through field reads
// and writes to the loads it was put together from. A register made any other way may be one, so it
// answers yes; a constant answers no.
private fed_from(defs: Map[string, Inst], reach: Reach, v: Val, s: string, depth: int) -> bool
    if depth > 64 then return true

    v match
        VReg(_) -> ()
        _ -> return false

    defs.get(v_render(v)) match
        Some(InLoad(_, _, p, _, _)) -> rooted_at(defs, reach, p, s)
        Some(InExtract(_, _, agg, _)) -> fed_from(defs, reach, agg, s, depth + 1)
        Some(InInsert(_, _, agg, _, value, _)) -> fed_from(defs, reach, agg, s, depth + 1) ||
                                                    fed_from(defs, reach, value, s, depth + 1)
        _ -> true
end fed_from

// Whether `inst` can neither read a count nor act on what one says. **A count can be read**: storage
// is let go of by `slot_vacate` only where the strong count is one, so a share dropped from inside
// the window would let it free slots the view still reads. That read is a load straight through an
// owner, never through a field address, so what may sit in the window is: a load of a stack slot, a
// global or a field (`getelementptr`); arithmetic and aggregate work; a count's own retain or
// release; an intrinsic, the bounds report or the stop a hosted trap goes through (it flushes C's
// streams and never returns); and a call to a function that releases nothing and writes nothing but
// its own locals.
count_blind(defs: Map[string, Inst], inert: Set[string], inst: Inst) -> bool = inst match
    InLoad(_, _, p, acc, _) if is_plain_access(acc) -> p match
        VGlobal(_) -> true
        VGep(_, _, _) -> true
        _ -> defs.get(v_render(p)) match
            Some(InAlloca(_, _, _)) -> true
            Some(InGep(_, _, _, _)) -> true
            Some(InGepInBounds(_, _, _, _)) -> true
            // A place entry answers a field, element or payload address -- never an owner's
            // (`place_entry.sysl`) -- so a load through it is a field read.
            Some(InCall(_, _, VGlobal(callee), _, _, _, _, _)) -> is_place_symbol(callee)
            _ -> false
    InLoad(_, _, _, _, _) -> false
    InCall(_, _, VGlobal(name), _, _, _, _, _) ->
        arc_call_of(inst).is_some() && release_for(name).is_some() ||
            name.starts_with("llvm.") || name == "sysl_bounds_fail" || name == trap_hook_symbol() ||
            name.starts_with("sysl.check.") || name == trap_stop_symbol() || name == bounds_stub_symbol() ||
            inert.has(name)
    // A call through a table's +0 slot: every body such a slot holds is inert, and so is the
    // forwarder in front of it (`table_zero.sysl`).
    InCall(_, _, VReg(r), _, _, _, _, _) -> is_zero_symbol(r)
    InCall(_, _, _, _, _, _, _, _) -> false
    InAsm(_, _, _, _, _) -> false
    InAtomicRmw(_, _, _, _, _, _) -> false
    InCmpXchg(_, _, _, _, _, _) -> false
    InFence(_) -> false
    InVaArg(_, _, _) -> false
    _ -> true

// Whether `inst` hands the thread to other code before it comes back: a coroutine's suspension point,
// or the resumption of the task being awaited. That code is any task of the domain, which may write the
// place a share was read out of and give back what it held, and may look at a count.
private suspends(inst: Inst) -> bool = inst match
    InCall(_, _, VGlobal(name), _, _, _, _, _) -> name.starts_with("llvm.coro.")
    _ -> false

// Whether a release of a reference from `o` gives back the count `c` took: it is the very value the
// retain was handed, it was put into a value by one of the retain's own field writes, or it was read
// out of the slot that value was stored into.
private gives_back(defs: Map[string, Inst], c: Cover, o: Origin) -> bool
    if o.leaf == c.leaf && o.path == c.path
        // The very value the retain was handed, read by the same instruction: one reference.
        if o.through == "" then return true

        for n in c.inserts
            if o.through.contains(s"|$n|") then return true

    c.into != "" && o.through == "" && loaded_slot(defs, o.leaf) == c.into && o.path == c.into_path
end gives_back
